\section{Thanks to}

Normally, thanks to are always at the end of each paper,
but the people or organizations I benefited from while trying to make AES strong again
are more important than a simple proof of concept showing that it works, except on my
raw experimental test form.

\href{https://www.bouncycastle.org/}{bouncycastle.org}

\href{https://www.schneier.com/}{schneier.com}

\href{https://github.com/dotnet/}{github.com/dotnet}

\href{https://github.com/microsoft}{github.com/microsoft}

\href{https://git.lysator.liu.se/nettle/nettle}{git.lysator.liu.se/nettle/nettle} (real easy to read c/c++ code)

Go to \href{https://io.cqrxs.eu/download/}{io.cqrxs.eu/download} and choose latest version.
Attention, version before March 2025 have a 3-fish over Aes-Engine encryption bug, because 3-fish
uses AES default block size and key length and Bouncy Castle Aes-Engine parameters. It works, but
settings AES default engine for 3-fish, isn’t so serious and please download version after March 30.


\section{Documentation online en-/decrypt form}

\begin{figure}
\includegraphics[width=0.2\textwidth,natwidth=924,natheight=659]{Symmetric_Cipher_WebForm.jpg}
\caption{\label{fig:SymmetricCipherWebForm}Symmetric Cipher WebForm}
\end{figure}

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Key: When clicking key your entered key will be stored temporary in session.
    \item Textbox secret key: Enter your Email address and secret key.
    \item Buton Clear: Clear and reset the entire form.
    \item Hyperlink Help: Show this help
    \item RadioButtonList KeyHashes
Choose the hash method to hash your secret key.
    \item ImageButton Hash: Clicking will hash your key and display hashed key in textbox.    
    \item TextBox Hash (readonly): Displays your hashed key.
    \item Button “Set Pipe”: sets symmetric cipher pipe, dependent only on your entered key
    \item Button “Hash Pipe”: sets symmetric cipher pipe, dependent primary on calculated hash
and secondary on your entered key.
    \item DropDown ZipTypes Choose encryption type (Please only GZip or Zip or None)
    \item DropDown CipherTypes Choose a symmetric cipher to add it to the symmetric cipher
pipe.
    \item ImageButton „add algo“: Clicking on will add the in c. DropDown CipherTypes
selected symmetric cipher algorithm to CipherPipe.
    \item TextBox CipherPipe (readonly): Displays the current Cipher Pipe algorithms.
    \item ImageButton “Clear Pipe”: Clicking on will clear only the entire Cipher Pipe
    \item DropDown EncodingTypes: Choose the final binary to ascii encoder, default is Base64.
Beware of using uuencode in Web, because <> will be interpreted as possible html
injection.
    \item TextArea Source: paste or enter Text here.
    \item TextArea Destination: (readonly) After clicking Encrypt or Decrypt processed text will
appear in the text area.
    \item Button Encrypt: Encrypts the text from TextArea Source and displays encrypted text in
TextArea Destination.
    \item Button “Random Text”: Adds a short fortune to TextArea Source.
    \item Button Decrypt: Decrypts text in TextArea Source and display decrypted text in
TextArea Destination.
\end{enumerate}


